            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function.\n\nHere's how it works:\n\n- **Semaphore**: Limits concurrent tasks using `asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrent)`\n- **Concurrency control**: Each task acquires/releases the semaphore, so only N run at a time\n- **Graceful shutdown**: When you press Ctrl+C:\n  1. All tasks are cancelled (raising `CancelledError` in them)\n  2. `gather(..., return_exceptions=True)` waits for all tasks to finish their cleanup\n  3. The `KeyboardInterrupt` is re-raised to the caller\n\nThis ensures `try/finally` blocks in your tasks run even during interruption."
